WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.133
- Nice to see you.

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:01.966
- Nice to see you too.

00:00:01.966 --> 00:00:04.770
You know, I may not be from
Texas, but my dad actually is.

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:05.790
- Oh, really? Where?

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:06.623
Do you know?
- So there we go.

00:00:06.623 --> 00:00:09.090
He's from Johnson County.

00:00:09.090 --> 00:00:10.020
- What?

00:00:10.020 --> 00:00:11.392
Are you (beep) right now?

00:00:11.392 --> 00:00:12.225
- No, I'm dead serious.

00:00:12.225 --> 00:00:13.200
I'm from Johnson and Tarrant.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:14.033
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:00:14.033 --> 00:00:15.537
I lived in both growing up. Yeah.

00:00:15.537 --> 00:00:17.460
- So, I didn't really
know my father very much.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.520
- Okay. Me neither.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:20.250
High five.
- Hey.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.083
- Hey therapy.
(audience laughs)

00:00:21.083 --> 00:00:21.916
- But I do know that's where he is from.

00:00:21.916 --> 00:00:23.109
Yeah, exactly.

00:00:23.109 --> 00:00:24.669
- That's awesome.
- That's where I am right now.

00:00:24.669 --> 00:00:25.502
This is therapy, right?

00:00:25.502 --> 00:00:26.335
- This is therapy.
- Oh, thank God.

00:00:26.335 --> 00:00:27.168
- Welcome to my couch.

00:00:27.168 --> 00:00:29.640
Yeah. I can talk a lot
about that issue, but--

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.620
No, but you had a mini
Dawson's Creek reunion

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:32.550
with Michelle, right?

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:33.407
At the Oscars.
- I did, yeah.

00:00:33.407 --> 00:00:35.011
- How is that?
(audience cheering)

00:00:35.011 --> 00:00:35.844
Like when you run into each other?

00:00:35.844 --> 00:00:36.677
- [Audience Member] Pacey!

00:00:36.677 --> 00:00:38.220
- Yes. Okay. Excited.
- Thank you, darling.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:39.900
- It's still very excited.
It's twenty years, though.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:40.931
That's a crazy amount of time.

00:00:40.931 --> 00:00:41.909
- Twenty five, I think.

00:00:41.909 --> 00:00:42.780
- Oh, twenty five.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:43.613
- Yeah.
- Wow.

00:00:43.613 --> 00:00:44.520
Over twenty years. Look how serious.

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.216
- [Joshua] It was a little
bit less gray on the beard.

00:00:46.216 --> 00:00:47.437
- What is she saying?
- She was saying,

00:00:47.437 --> 00:00:49.658
"I can't believe you're a father".

00:00:49.658 --> 00:00:51.210
(laughing)

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:52.260
- No, but that's what's so cool.

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:54.300
Like years later, you
knew each other so young.

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.650
- [Joshua] Yeah. And you were the kids.

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:56.580
- Yeah.
- Yeah.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:00:59.160
I mean this, we don't get to
see each other all that often.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:00.720
She has her kids, she lives in New York.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.400
I have my kid, we live here.

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:03.810
But that was a lovely night

00:01:03.810 --> 00:01:05.550
and just having the
opportunity to see her.

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:07.710
I hadn't met her new husband
since they got together.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:08.543
- [Kelly] Oh, yeah.

00:01:08.543 --> 00:01:10.260
- Who's the third person
in that photograph.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.700
So, yeah, I mean, it's a funny thing

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.520
to get like the most fancy dress up party

00:01:14.520 --> 00:01:15.390
that you can possibly do

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:17.220
and then have a high school
reunion, but that's what we did.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:19.647
- Yeah. I love that, though. It's fun.

